                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e44d83d0-32ef-3906-821c-4a43e73823a3",
                        "entry_id": "6247896e-9e2b-3bb2-806e-94d69060ee05",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à la demisexualité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a26eda-c161-40f6-a3d9-48ebf78dc2cb",
                                "sense_id": "e44d83d0-32ef-3906-821c-4a43e73823a3",
                                "text": "Un nombre croissant d'ados refusent l'idée d'être homo ou hétéro, mais explorent des degrés de bisexualité. Un nouveau monde de nuances émerge, ou l'on peut se découvrir neutre, pansexuel, cisgenré, transgenre, demisexuel, grissexuel, aromantique, gynesexuel ou genderfluid..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83da1756-b53f-40dd-99e6-71c7d126bab9",
                                "sense_id": "e44d83d0-32ef-3906-821c-4a43e73823a3",
                                "text": "Alors comment savoir si vous êtes demisexuel ? Demandez-vous si, lorsque vous croisez quelqu'un dans la rue, à la télé ou n'importe où, vous ressentez une attraction physique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a34ba007-e5ae-4d85-a236-d4185a8c0c06",
                        "source_entry_id": "6247896e-9e2b-3bb2-806e-94d69060ee05",
                        "source_sense_id": "e44d83d0-32ef-3906-821c-4a43e73823a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "demisexual",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "demisexual",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32abf01f-c6af-3696-96d1-450548b660df",
                                        "entry_id": "16d94a53-a036-3203-9e58-c11b5b7ad61d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexually attracted to people only after a strong emotional bond has been formed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of humans"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "874cca6f-0c6e-4071-951b-80b3690cb0dd",
                                                "sense_id": "32abf01f-c6af-3696-96d1-450548b660df",
                                                "text": "Some people may identify as asexual for a period and then decide that they are in fact demisexual, or even sexual."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2e50db6-949b-4037-9d57-08e50814eedb",
                                                "sense_id": "32abf01f-c6af-3696-96d1-450548b660df",
                                                "text": "Some think of themselves as demisexual, only able to feel attraction when a very strong emotional bond already exists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d0f845e-2439-45fd-a179-582e714a32bc",
                                                "sense_id": "32abf01f-c6af-3696-96d1-450548b660df",
                                                "text": "In asexual / ace communities in the past few years, there has been an enormous increase in prominence of people identifying as gray-A and as demisexual, with ‘ace’ now sometimes being used as an umbrella term."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "demisexual",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "018f522d-1d2e-39eb-843c-f0b215a965af",
                                        "entry_id": "9b575137-ea26-3af3-80f9-859621bdf19c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who is demisexual."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cacff3e1-624b-4b9b-87ed-1d30482cb7be",
                                                "sense_id": "018f522d-1d2e-39eb-843c-f0b215a965af",
                                                "text": "Demisexuals experience sexual attraction as a consequence of romantic attraction but not independently of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba3c9dcc-728a-40fb-9b66-2d9785fd8b4e",
                                                "sense_id": "018f522d-1d2e-39eb-843c-f0b215a965af",
                                                "text": "Demisexuals experience sexual desire only toward people with whom they already have a strong emotional bond. Like an asexual, a demisexual would not see an attractive woman and immediately desire sex, unless, of course, that attractive woman happened to be in a serious emotional relationship with the demisexual."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a99fb667-4fe6-4af0-b541-12f6f84a4d61",
                                                "sense_id": "018f522d-1d2e-39eb-843c-f0b215a965af",
                                                "text": "Rines identified himself as a demisexual, meaning that he is only sexually attracted to a person once a strong emotional attachment has been formed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
